findings.body:
This PR's rename changed the opencode-plugin copy action in `src/plan.utils.ts` (and the matching `WIRING` entry in `src/cli.ts:234`) from referencing `agent-init.js` to `agentspine.js`:

```ts
actions.push({
  kind: "copy",
  target: ".opencode/plugins/agentspine.js",
  from: path.join(templates, "agents/plugins/opencode/agentspine.js"),
});
```

But the actual template file on disk was never renamed — it's still `templates/agents/plugins/opencode/agent-init.js` (only its contents were edited; `git diff --name-status` shows `M`, not a rename). No `agentspine.js` file exists anywhere under `templates/agents/plugins/opencode/`.

`src/apply.utils.ts`'s `"copy"` case calls `cpSync(action.from, target)` with no try/catch, and the `--check` path (`wouldChange`) does `readFileSync(action.from, ...)` — both throw `ENOENT` on the missing source. Since `hooks` defaults to `true` (`src/cli.ts:58`), any `npx agentspine` run (or `--check`) with opencode detected or selected crashes instead of scaffolding. This also breaks the repo's own dogfood copy at `.opencode/plugins/agent-init.js` (never renamed) and its own `agentspine --check`/`doctor` gate, which `docs/design/0001-architecture.md`'s decision on that gate and this PR's own "Merge danger" section both point to as the safety net for exactly this class of drift.

The companion doc `templates/agents/plugins/opencode/README.md:3` was updated to say the plugin is "Copied to `.opencode/plugins/agentspine.js`" — describing a copy that cannot currently succeed.

Fix: rename `templates/agents/plugins/opencode/agent-init.js` to `agentspine.js` (and its exported `AgentInit` identifier for consistency), matching the paths already updated in `src/plan.utils.ts` and `src/cli.ts`.

